<body>
<h1>The Map Room</h1>
<p>The map room occupies the quiet end of the neighborhood library. Its shelves hold folded street plans, ferry schedules, and hand-drawn routes collected over several decades. A small brass weight keeps each sheet flat while readers compare editions.</p>
<p>Mara volunteers on Thursday afternoons. She records the paper&#39;s date, the names of its surveyors, and any handwritten notes near the margins. When a street changes, she adds a transparent overlay rather than altering the older map.</p>
<p>Visitors often arrive looking for one address and leave with a longer story. They discover a footbridge that no longer exists, a lane named after a vanished orchard, or a public stair hidden behind a market. The archive cannot answer every question, but it can show where to ask next.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Keep a note of what the map cannot show.</p>
</blockquote>
<pre><code class="language-text">copy → compare → annotate
</code></pre>
<p>A route index lives at <a href="https://example.org/index" rel="noopener noreferrer">https://example.org/index</a>.</p>
